t.ts` to count both endpoints for valid ascending integer ranges. Correct the `5..5` expectation and add a `1..3` assertion in `src/count.test.ts`; define and test the intended behavior for reversed and non-integer inputs before relying on the function more broadly. Rerun the direct check and `bun test`.\n+2. **Phase 2 — resolve and make the frontend audit verifiable:** Investigate the reported 21 high-severity advisories, including `@tiptap/core`, against an actual dependency inventory; remediate confirmed affected dependencies and replace the fixed-message `scripts/frontend-audit.ts` check with an audit that reports reproducible evidence and fails on actionable findings. Rerun `bun run verify` and document any remaining advisories and blockers without calling a failed audit a pass.\n*** End Patch"},"metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: <flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md\n===================================================================\n--- <flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md\n+++ <flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+# Codebase review and improvement roadmap\n+\n+## Current-source findings\n+\n+- **Correctness — inclusive interval count:** `src/count.ts` returns `end - start`, omitting one endpoint of a closed interval. A direct Bun invocation of `inclusiveRangeLength(1, 3)` produced:\n+\n+Finding: inclusiveRangeLength is incorrect for 1..3.\n+Actual: 2; Expected: 3\n+\n+- **Coverage — wrong expectation:** `src/count.test.ts` expects a zero-width closed interval `5..5` to contain zero integers; it should contain one. There is no test for a nonzero-width closed interval. `src/greet.test.ts` covers the one `greet` example and passes.\n+- **Audit — failing gate:** `scripts/frontend-audit.ts` reports **21 high-severity advisories, including `@tiptap/core`**, then exits with status 1. The script contains a fixed message and does not enumerate or dynamically verify the underlying advisories, so the individual adv